# Next.js (web) — copy to `.env.local`
# https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/configuring-environment-variables

# Sanity — project (required; same id as `studio/.env`).
# `next.config.ts` inlines `SANITY_STUDIO_*` into the **client** bundle (Next normally
# only inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`) so Client Components and the server resolve to the same
# project id and dataset — otherwise SSR + CSR produce different Sanity image URLs and
# React reports a hydration mismatch. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID` needed.
SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Dataset override (optional; `@repo/sanity-dataset-resolve` / `sanity/sanityEnv.ts`) ---
# Default: no vars — order is inferred (e.g. dev-first locally, prod-first on Vercel production).
#
# Single lever for development / preview deploys: set the SAME variable on the host (Vercel / Netlify /
# Docker env) for **web** and **studio** builds so both point at the same Content Lake dataset.
# - `production` | `development` | `preview` — built-in ordering (see package README).
# - Any other value (e.g. `development`) — try a dataset with that name first, then dev/prod fallbacks.
# SANITY_STUDIO_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=development
#
# Hard pin (skips auto-selection and `SANITY_STUDIO_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`).
# `next.config.ts` exposes this to the browser too — set it once.
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=

# Sanity — live preview & Visual Editing (Presentation, Draft Mode, Stega)
# Also used for **Site languages** (`siteLanguageSettings`): with a token, Next reads draft/unpublished
# settings so URLs and fallbacks match Studio before publish. Same token as Studio codegen optional.
SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_ORIGIN=
# Studio URL — click-to-edit links (Stega) and CSP `frame-ancestors`, so Presentation
# may embed this site. Default `http://localhost:3333`; `*.sanity.studio` is always
# allowed. In production, the Studio's hosting URL (`SANITY_STUDIO_HOSTING_URL` in
# `studio/.env`), e.g. its Netlify custom domain. Read at BUILD time.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STUDIO_URL=https://studio.your-domain.tld

# Sanity webhook secret for `/api/revalidate`. Set the same secret on the webhook in
# Sanity Manage → API → Webhooks; the route verifies its `sanity-webhook-signature` header.
# Required in production — the route refuses requests if this is unset when
# `NODE_ENV=production`. With it set, caches live until the webhook expires their tags and
# <SanityLive /> runs in Draft Mode only; without it <SanityLive /> runs for every visitor and
# published reads fall back to a 60 s window (see web/README.md, Freshness).
SANITY_REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# Public site URL — canonical origin for `metadataBase`, canonical/hreflang links,
# `og:url`, `sitemap.ts` and `robots.ts`. Resolved in `web/src/utils/siteUrl.ts`.
#
# Inlined at BUILD time, so it has to be set in the build environment (Netlify:
# `[context.production.environment]` in `netlify.toml`) — a runtime-only variable
# is too late. Left unset, the resolver falls back to the deploy host's own origin
# (Netlify `URL` / `DEPLOY_PRIME_URL`, Vercel `VERCEL_URL`) and, on a deploy host
# with neither, fails the build instead of publishing a placeholder. Locally,
# unset resolves to http://localhost:3000 — which is what you want for dev, so
# leave it commented out.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.tld

# Self-hosted analytics for the Content-Security-Policy (`web/next.config.ts`):
# comma-separated origins of a Matomo, Plausible or PostHog instance configured
# in Studio → Analytics. The cloud hosts of all supported providers are already
# allowed. Read at BUILD time, like the rest of `headers()`.
# CSP_ANALYTICS_ORIGINS=https://analytics.example.com
